# Form input guard (boss-web)

A global guard (`lib/latin-input.ts`, `GlobalLatinInputGuard`) strips non-Latin characters (Hangul/CJK/Cyrillic) from inputs as the user types. It auto-detects a mode from `type`/`name`/`id`, but detection defaults to `letters` and **will block digits/symbols** on generic fields.

## When adding or fixing an input

- If a field needs anything other than plain letters, set `data-latin-mode` explicitly. Available modes: `letters`, `email`, `password`, `tel`, `number`, `decimal`, `address`, `ascii`.
- Common fixes:
  - Item ID / SKU / search → `data-latin-mode="ascii"` (letters + digits + symbols).
  - Money / quantity that needs a decimal point → `data-latin-mode="decimal"`.
  - Whole numbers only → `data-latin-mode="number"`.
- For a numeric field that must accept decimals, also use `type="text"` + `inputMode="decimal"` and a draft string state. `type="number"` truncates/zero-pads decimals during typing.
- To opt a field out of the guard entirely, use `data-latin-input="off"` (on the field or an ancestor).

If a user reports "can't type numbers/letters in field X", it is almost always a missing `data-latin-mode`.
